{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1508875-htr-and-dtf-what-books-to-buy","id":1508875,"title":"HtR and DtF: what books to buy?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-19T04:38:55-07:00","id":1508875,"title":"HtR and DtF: what books to buy?","content":"I've decided I might as well round off the collection. So should I look for 20th anniversary translation guides on the vault, or just use the cores as is? (I seem to recall complaints about DtF rules being a bit of a mess)<br /> <br /> And as I know nothing about the existence of any books outside the core, are there any supplements you recommend getting (or avoiding)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T07:11:57-07:00","id":1508883,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Demon:_The_Fallen_books\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Demon:_The_Fallen_books<br /> <br /> https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hunter:_The_Reckoning_books</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","user":"Psicose","date":". 04-19-2023, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T07:57:36-07:00","id":1508889,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would pass on H:tR completely, even assume it didn't ever happen (that's the rule in my own World of Darkness) and take a look at most D:tF books.<br /> Concerning this game, The Earthbound is awesome to create antagonists that can be used in any of the game, including Mummy: the Resurrection.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;No, no, don't look any further, my profile is actually more handsome than me&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3586-alqamar-alaswad","name":"Alqamar Alaswad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"287"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T12:40:03-07:00","id":1508918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alqamar Alaswad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1508875-htr-and-dtf-what-books-to-buy?p=1508889#post1508889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I would pass on H:tR completely, even assume it didn't ever happen (that's the rule in my own World of Darkness) and take a look at most D:tF books.<br /> Concerning this game, The Earthbound is awesome to create antagonists that can be used in any of the game, including Mummy: the Resurrection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter: the Reckoning 1e is actually an interesting concept with promise, if you can distance yourself from the idea that hunters should be normal humans. Take what are essentially Solar Exaltations, but a load of limiters on them, and give them to people who create something one part fundementalist army of god to one part 4chan. It's much, much more interesting than the second edition being 'Hunters Hunted, but without Numina or Org membership'.<br /> <br /> DtF is excellent though, I should really get more than just the core. Sadly I'm too unlikely to ever run it to justify that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T14:08:37-07:00","id":1508925,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar27832_1.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27832\" data-vbnamecard=\"27832\">Psicose</a> Your links merged and just link to the DtF book list.<br /> <br /> -----------------<br /> <br /> On DtF:<br /> <br /> Given how many holes there are in the core book... you basically want all the gaming supplements. There's a few you can skip if they're not your thing (City of Angels and Fear to Tread, which are a combo, have some useful lore tidbits in them, but you're not missing out on some important rules expansions, Saviors and Destroys, and Damned and Deceived aren't bad per se, but you probably aren't going to use the much), but all of them at least add something to the game.<br /> <br /> On HtR:<br /> <br /> The core book is more solid on its own; just ignore the art. The important thing is to pay attention to the &quot;optional&quot; Conviction rewards and consider them &quot;situational&quot; rewards because without those the Conviction economy of the game is exceedingly hard to manage. The overall HtR book list has a lot more stuff in it (DtF put all the Houses in one book, while HtR gave each Creed its own). Like DtF most of the books are useful, though some may or may not appeal to you (the&quot;enemy&quot; books specifically that deal with running other parts of the WoD more in-line with their own game-line presentations, except Fall from Grace which covers both demons and some important high-level Imbued play options). <br /> <br /> The Players Guide, ST Handbook, ST Companion, and Urban Legends are probably the most essential supplements (esp, some of the optional rules for PCs, and expanded rules for Bystanders, NPC Creeds, and more monster building tools); HtR (and DtF since it largely copied from HtR) has a really weird Merits and Flaws section that's not necessarily bad but has very different assumptions than the previous games. The Creedbooks are generally solid. Their fiction can be eh, but most have some useful stuff in them. Beware the Ability and Background bloat (most of them introduce a few of each), a lot of them just aren't that important. Also be careful if you're using the baseline advancement rules because the increased Edge options tempt players into traps where they end up locking themselves out of high level powers if they're not careful.<br /> <br /> The two big books to be careful with are Utopia and Holy War. Utopia is... well not good. The authors have long since revealed that they were told to sabotage the book because they weren't allowed to let the Imbued &quot;win.&quot; So a book that's supposed to examine what happens if the Imbued manage to get their act together and start working more effectively as a unified community, turns into an exercise in cynicism and fatalism as all the options are doomed to fail by editorial fiat. There are some interesting ideas, but you need to sift through at lot of cruft to get to them. Holy War is racist and Islamophobic. It is one of the worst failures in the cWoD in this regard. It might not be the worst,but it's bad. It's also bad on a meta-level because a ton of well written stuff by a Muslim freelancer got edited into the tone of the rest of the book to try to make it look not-bigoted. While there are some diamonds in the rough along the lines of Utopia... its a lot less worth buying to get them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T15:05:31-07:00","id":1508930,"title":"","content":"I would heavily recommend HTR 1st Edition Core and Fall From Grace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27335-technoma","name":"Technoma","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T02:15:53-07:00","id":1509010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1508875-htr-and-dtf-what-books-to-buy?p=1508918#post1508918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take what are essentially Solar Exaltations, but a load of limiters on them, and give them to people who create something one part fundementalist army of god to one part 4chan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of this, in my own metaplot Solars eventually returned due to Messengers think imbued isn't enough/The One Above finally takes the whole thing, and did the real Recknoing (No other Exs though), specific time varies, from Week of Nightmare when they appeared and killed Ravnos instead, to simply a few years ago, but Imbueds still exist, as a secondary splat like ghouls (for Bystanders I leave them blank, maybe still exists too or simply be removed)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T06:26:50-07:00","id":1509032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1508875-htr-and-dtf-what-books-to-buy?p=1509010#post1509010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of this, in my own metaplot Solars eventually returned due to Messengers think imbued isn't enough/The One Above finally takes the whole thing, and did the real Recknoing (No other Exs though), specific time varies, from Week of Nightmare when they appeared and killed Ravnos instead, to simply a few years ago, but Imbueds still exist, as a secondary splat like ghouls (for Bystanders I leave them blank, maybe still exists too or simply be removed)</div> </div> </div> </div>You could also do what Ex2 did with Bystanders - make them how you get Infernals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-20T06:44:35-07:00","id":1509035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1508875-htr-and-dtf-what-books-to-buy?p=1509010#post1509010\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of this, in my own metaplot Solars eventually returned due to Messengers think imbued isn't enough/The One Above finally takes the whole thing, and did the real Recknoing (No other Exs though), specific time varies, from Week of Nightmare when they appeared and killed Ravnos instead, to simply a few years ago, but Imbueds still exist, as a secondary splat like ghouls (for Bystanders I leave them blank, maybe still exists too or simply be removed)</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal version replaced Reckoning with Vigil, but the Imbued are still around as a (currently NPC-only) Conspiracy. Full on Exalts aren't a thing, but that's mostly because I'm not familiar enough with Exalted to do them justice. Reckoning being replaced is less because it's bad and more me really quite liking the Vigil conspiracies.<br /> <br /> Bystanders probably just fade into the normal mortal hunter community after a while, the Masquerade/Veil/whatever was never THAT strong to begin with. In the long run there's not much difference between a failed imbuing and everybody else who knows about the supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-18T04:08:22-07:00","id":1522741,"title":"","content":"Considering your desire to round off your collection, the 20th-anniversary translation guides can enhance your experience, particularly for &quot;Demon: The Fallen.&quot; Supplements like &quot;Hunter: The Infernal&quot; or &quot;Demon Players Guide&quot; can add depth to your campaigns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28202-karajoe","user":"KaraJoe","date":". 10-19-2023, 09:21 AM"},"a